Modelica source:
```modelica
connector Port
  Real e;
  flow Real f;
end Port;
model Leaf
  Port p;
end Leaf;
model TargetHub
  Port anchor;
  Leaf a;
  Leaf b;
equation
  connect(anchor,a.p);
end TargetHub;
model DistractorHub
  Port anchor;
  Leaf a;
  Leaf b;
equation
  connect(anchor,a.p);
  connect(a.p,b.p);
end DistractorHub;
model Study
  TargetHub targetHub;
  DistractorHub distractor;
end Study;
```

Question:
Within the equation scope of model instance Study.targetHub, return the canonical signed member vector for the primitive flow connection set generated there that contains targetHub.anchor.f.

Target:
targetHub.anchor.f

Answer format:
Use ascending path:integer entries joined by commas without spaces; coefficients must be primitive, nonzero, and oriented so the first coefficient is positive.
Return exactly {"answer":"..."}.
